% A constraint over a negated derived predicate: every reviewed change must
% have an approval, directly or through a delegate.  The negated predicate
% sits in a lower stratum and is complete when the constraint runs.
change(c1).
change(c2).
change(c3).
approved(c1, ann).
delegate(c2, c1).
ok(C) :- approved(C, _).
ok(C) :- delegate(C, D), ok(D).
:- change(C), not ok(C).
